.SH COMMANDS
.PP
Target filesystem helpers retain logical metadata separately from writable staging:
target_extract_tar(archive, root), target_extract_rpm(archive, root),
target_capture_apks(root, archive_directories), target_mode(root, relative_path, mode)
and target_finalize(root). RPM extraction requires the image's rpm/rpm2archive;
it does not run package scriptlets. Capture package metadata before policy,
then finalize the tree after policy changes.
target_extract_rpm(archive, root, members) also writes the record of the
extraction to members, from which a package is composed into another root.
target_pack_tree(root, archive) moves a staging tree, its modes, times, links
and target metadata manifest, into a new tar archive, removing root;
target_unpack_tree(archive, root) makes that tree again under an empty root.
See docs/target-metadata.md.
exec returns a status; exec_checked and exec_output fail on nonzero exit.
Their optional options map accepts child-only cwd and env. Shell strings need
proper quoting and checked pipelines. Diagnostics go to stderr.
.SH OUTPUTS
Use ctx.runtime.paths.build for work and ctx.runtime.paths.tools for shared
dependency tools. Inputs are immutable below /inputs. The owned target is /out.
Select real files/directories in ctx.outputs; the coordinator validates them
before publication and returns their published host paths in the final context.
.SH ACQUISITION
Downloads require SHA256 and replace a valid destination only after complete
verification. Git acquisition requires an exact destination and full commit id.
Every redirect endpoint also needs a network grant. Package facts stay in Rhai.
